---
import '../../styles/global.css';

const talks = [
  { number: '01', title: 'The Room Before the Room', body: 'How leaders create the conditions for a consequential conversation before the agenda begins.' },
  { number: '02', title: 'Pressure Without Performance', body: 'A working session on speaking with precision when the stakes are real and the answer is not obvious.' },
  { number: '03', title: 'The Decision Lives Here', body: 'A structured keynote that turns communication from a soft skill into an operating behavior.' },
];

const method = [
  ['Notice', 'Read the pressure already active in the room before choosing the message.'],
  ['Name', 'Give the decision a clear language that people can carry after the session.'],
  ['Rehearse', 'Build the behaviors that make a message usable under real conditions.'],
  ['Return', 'Leave leaders with a move they can make in the next consequential room.'],
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="obsidian-gold">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Elena Voss — Authority + Speaking | AURA Concept</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="description" content="A concept-safe Authority + Speaking archetype preview compiled by AURA." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://raydenai.github.io/archetypes/authority-speaking/" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,600;9..40,700&family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,500;0,600;1,500;1,600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body class="authority-preview">
    <a class="as-skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <header class="as-header">
      <a class="as-wordmark" href="/archetypes/authority-speaking/">ELENA VOSS<span>LEADERSHIP COMMUNICATION</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Preview navigation">
        <a href="#method">THE METHOD</a>
        <a href="#outcomes">OUTCOMES</a>
        <a href="#speaking">SPEAKING</a>
      </nav>
      <a class="as-header-cta" href="#inquiry">CHECK AVAILABILITY <span>↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="as-hero">
        <img class="as-hero-image" src="/images/authority-speaking-hero.webp" alt="Conceptual leadership communication adviser standing near an empty auditorium stage." width="1920" height="1080" />
        <div class="as-hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="as-hero-copy">
          <p class="as-kicker">AUTHORITY + SPEAKING <i></i> CONCEPT PREVIEW</p>
          <h1>THE ROOM<br />FEELS YOU<br /><em>BEFORE</em> IT<br />HEARS YOU.</h1>
          <p class="as-intro">A keynote is not a performance slot. It is a rehearsal for the decision your leaders need to make next.</p>
          <div class="as-hero-actions">
            <a class="as-button as-button--light" href="#inquiry">CHECK SPEAKING AVAILABILITY <span>↗</span></a>
            <a class="as-text-link" href="#method">EXPLORE THE LIVE ROOM METHOD <span>↓</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="as-hero-side">FOR LEADERSHIP ROOMS WITH SOMETHING AT STAKE <span>01 / 06</span></div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-concept-note">
        <span>CONCEPT-SAFE PREVIEW</span>
        <p>Elena Voss, the photography, and all speaking contexts on this page are fictional AURA test material. The page shows the compiled <strong>Authority + Speaking</strong> system—not real events, clients, results, or endorsements.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="as-outcomes" id="outcomes">
        <div class="as-section-label"><span>01</span> WHAT A ROOM LEAVES WITH</div>
        <div class="as-outcomes-head" data-reveal>
          <p class="as-eyebrow">THE EVENT-BUYER QUESTION</p>
          <h2>NOT "WAS IT<br /><em>INSPIRING?"</em></h2>
          <p>The better question is: what will a leader say, notice, or do differently in the next hard room?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="as-outcomes-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>A SHARED LANGUAGE</h3><p>One useful sentence can change the quality of a team’s next disagreement.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>A PRACTICAL MOVE</h3><p>A serious session leaves people with behavior, not a borrowed feeling.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>A BETTER QUESTION</h3><p>When the pressure rises, a better question creates a better decision.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-story">
        <div class="as-story-image-wrap"><img src="/images/authority-speaking-work.webp" alt="Conceptual adviser preparing a leadership communication framework at a table." width="1600" height="1067" /><span>THE WORK BEFORE THE ROOM</span></div>
        <div class="as-story-copy" data-reveal>
          <p class="as-eyebrow">THE POINT OF VIEW</p>
          <h2>THE MOST<br />IMPORTANT<br /><em>CONVERSATION</em><br />STARTS BEFORE<br />ANYONE SPEAKS.</h2>
          <p>Most leadership events begin with a topic. The Live Room Method begins with the decision, pressure, and behavior already waiting underneath it.</p>
          <p class="as-small">This is a test concept. A live build would replace this language only after the speaker’s actual expertise, proof, topic outcomes, and event logistics are approved in the Evidence Register.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-method" id="method">
        <div class="as-method-top">
          <div class="as-section-label"><span>02</span> THE LIVE ROOM METHOD</div>
          <p>The Authority + Speaking compiler selects a room-first sequence: establish relevance, earn trust, show the point of view, specify the event format, then request booking context.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="as-method-list">
          {method.map(([title, body], index) => <article data-reveal><span>0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-speaker-image">
        <img src="/images/authority-speaking-stage.webp" alt="Conceptual adviser walking across an empty theatre stage under an amber spotlight." width="1920" height="1080" />
        <div><span>03 / CONTEXT, NOT CLAIM</span><p>The stage image is a required photography role for this architecture. In a live build, it must be a real permissioned event image or labelled as an approved concept—not borrowed authority.</p></div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-talks" id="speaking">
        <div class="as-talks-head" data-reveal><p class="as-eyebrow">SPEAKING TOPICS</p><h2>THREE WAYS<br />TO CHANGE<br /><em>THE ROOM.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="as-talk-list">
          {talks.map((talk) => <article><span>{talk.number}</span><div><h3>{talk.title}</h3><p>{talk.body}</p></div><a href="#inquiry" aria-label={`Ask about ${talk.title}`}>↗</a></article>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="as-inquiry" id="inquiry">
        <div class="as-inquiry-copy" data-reveal>
          <p class="as-eyebrow">EVENT INQUIRY</p>
          <h2>START WITH<br />THE <em>ROOM.</em></h2>
          <p>Tell us what the event needs to make possible. The right topic, format, and work begin there.</p>
          <img src="/images/authority-speaking-close.webp" alt="Conceptual close editorial portrait of the fictional leadership communication adviser." width="1200" height="1500" />
        </div>
        <form class="as-form" action="#" method="post" data-demo-form>
          <p>This is a non-collecting concept form. It displays the exact booking context selected by the Authority + Speaking Compiler.</p>
          <label>YOUR NAME <input name="name" type="text" placeholder="Name" /></label>
          <label>WORK EMAIL <input name="email" type="email" placeholder="you@organization.com" /></label>
          <label>ORGANIZATION <input name="organization" type="text" placeholder="Organization" /></label>
          <div class="as-form-pair"><label>EVENT DATE <input name="event_date" type="text" placeholder="Month / year" /></label><label>AUDIENCE SIZE <input name="audience_size" type="text" placeholder="Approx. size" /></label></div>
          <div class="as-form-pair"><label>FORMAT <input name="format" type="text" placeholder="Keynote / workshop" /></label><label>BUDGET RANGE <input name="budget_range" type="text" placeholder="Optional range" /></label></div>
          <label>DESIRED OUTCOME <textarea name="desired_outcome" rows="3" placeholder="What should be different after the room?" /></label>
          <button type="submit">CHECK AVAILABILITY <span>↗</span></button>
        </form>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="as-footer"><span>ELENA VOSS / AURA AUTHORITY + SPEAKING CONCEPT</span><span>COMPILED FROM A CONCEPT-SAFE CLIENT PACK</span></footer>

    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLFormElement>('[data-demo-form]').forEach((form) => form.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        alert('Concept preview only — no information is collected. A live client build connects this validated field set to the approved contact backend.');
      }));
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => entries.forEach((entry) => entry.isIntersecting && entry.target.setAttribute('data-visible', 'true')), { threshold: 0.1 });
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach((element) => observer.observe(element));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; background: #10100f; }
  :global(body.authority-preview) { margin: 0; background: #10100f; color: #f4eee2; font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; }
  .as-skip { position: fixed; left: 1rem; top: -4rem; z-index: 20; background: #e5c07a; color: #161411; padding: .7rem 1rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .as-skip:focus { top: 1rem; }
  .as-header { height: 82px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 0 3.2vw; position: absolute; width: 100%; z-index: 5; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(238,225,199,.18); }
  .as-wordmark { color: #f6efe2; font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace; font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .13em; font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; line-height: 1.2; }
  .as-wordmark span { display: block; color: #bdb2a0; letter-spacing: .12em; font-size: .52rem; margin-top: .35rem; }
  nav { display: flex; gap: 2rem; } nav a { color: #dfd5c5; text-decoration: none; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .14em; font-weight: 600; }
  .as-header-cta, .as-button { display: inline-flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; background: #e1bc6a; color: #171511; text-decoration: none; padding: .9rem 1.2rem; font-size: .62rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; }
  .as-header-cta span, .as-button span { font-size: 1rem; }
  .as-hero { min-height: 850px; position: relative; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; overflow: hidden; background: #11100e; }
  .as-hero-image { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center; }
  .as-hero-overlay { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(11,10,8,.94) 0%, rgba(11,10,8,.68) 39%, rgba(11,10,8,.10) 74%), linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(11,10,8,.6), transparent 46%); }
  .as-hero-copy { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: min(670px, 52vw); padding: 0 0 8rem 7.5vw; }
  .as-kicker, .as-eyebrow { color: #e1bc6a; font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace; font-weight: 500; font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .17em; margin: 0 0 1.6rem; }
  .as-kicker i { display: inline-block; width: 38px; height: 1px; background: #e1bc6a; vertical-align: middle; margin: 0 .55rem; }
  h1, h2, h3, p { margin-top: 0; } h1 { font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(3.55rem, 7.5vw, 7.5rem); line-height: .82; letter-spacing: -.085em; margin: 0; max-width: 680px; font-weight: 700; }
  h1 em, h2 em { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.07em; }
  .as-intro { color: #ded4c6; max-width: 480px; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 2.4rem 0; }
  .as-hero-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .as-text-link { font-size: .65rem; color: #f5eee1; text-decoration: none; letter-spacing: .12em; font-weight: 600; }.as-text-link span { color: #e1bc6a; margin-left: .5rem; }
  .as-hero-side { position: absolute; z-index: 1; right: 3vw; bottom: 2.5rem; writing-mode: vertical-rl; font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace; font-size: .56rem; letter-spacing: .13em; color: #c7bbab; display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: center; }.as-hero-side span { color: #e1bc6a; }
  .as-concept-note { background: #e1bc6a; color: #161411; padding: 1.2rem 7.5vw; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 180px minmax(0, 800px); gap: 2rem; font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.55; }.as-concept-note span { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:.57rem; letter-spacing:.13em; font-weight:700; padding-top:.2rem; }.as-concept-note p { margin: 0; }
  .as-outcomes { padding: 8rem 7.5vw; background: #f0ebe0; color: #161411; }.as-section-label { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.12em; display:flex; gap:1rem; align-items:center; color:#746e66; }.as-section-label span { color:#a8782c; }.as-outcomes-head { display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr .7fr; column-gap: 3rem; padding: 5rem 0 4.5rem; align-items:end; }.as-outcomes-head .as-eyebrow { grid-column:1 / -1; color:#a8782c; }.as-outcomes h2, .as-story h2, .as-talks h2, .as-inquiry h2 { font-size:clamp(2.8rem,5.8vw,6rem); line-height:.88; letter-spacing:-.075em; margin:0; font-weight:700; }.as-outcomes-head > p:last-child { margin:0; font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.65; color:#514c46; max-width:340px; }.as-outcomes-grid { border-top:1px solid #cfc7b9; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr); }.as-outcomes-grid article { padding:2rem 2rem 0 0; margin-right:2rem; min-height:190px; border-right:1px solid #d5cec1; }.as-outcomes-grid article:last-child { border:0; }.as-outcomes-grid span { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:.65rem; color:#a8782c; }.as-outcomes-grid h3 { font-size:1rem; letter-spacing:.05em; margin:3.2rem 0 .7rem; }.as-outcomes-grid p { color:#5c554c; line-height:1.6; font-size:.88rem; }
  .as-story { padding:8rem 7.5vw; background:#171614; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr; gap:9vw; align-items:center; }.as-story-image-wrap { position:relative; }.as-story-image-wrap img { display:block;width:100%; aspect-ratio:3/2; object-fit:cover; }.as-story-image-wrap span { position:absolute; bottom:1rem; left:1rem; color:#ede5d8; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:.55rem; letter-spacing:.14em; }.as-story-copy { max-width:540px; }.as-story-copy h2 { color:#f2ebdf; }.as-story-copy .as-eyebrow { color:#e1bc6a; }.as-story-copy > p { margin:2rem 0 0; line-height:1.7; font-size:1.05rem; color:#c9c1b7; }.as-story-copy .as-small { font-size:.76rem; color:#918a80; max-width:430px; }
  .as-method { padding:8rem 7.5vw 7rem; background:#11100f; }.as-method-top { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:4rem; border-bottom:1px solid #38352f; padding-bottom:4rem; }.as-method-top p { max-width:450px; margin:0; color:#b6aea2; font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.7; }.as-method-list { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); }.as-method-list article { padding:2rem 2rem 1rem 0; border-right:1px solid #38352f; min-height:240px; opacity:0; transform:translateY(12px); transition:.6s ease; }.as-method-list article[data-visible] { opacity:1; transform:none; }.as-method-list article+article { padding-left:2rem; }.as-method-list article:last-child { border:0; }.as-method-list span { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:.62rem; color:#e1bc6a; }.as-method-list h3 { color:#f0e9de; margin:4rem 0 .8rem; letter-spacing:.05em; font-size:1rem; }.as-method-list p { color:#a49c91; font-size:.82rem; line-height:1.65; }
  .as-speaker-image { position:relative; min-height:680px; overflow:hidden; }.as-speaker-image > img { position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover; }.as-speaker-image:after { content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(0,0,0,.7),transparent 60%); }.as-speaker-image > div { position:absolute;z-index:1;left:7.5vw;bottom:4.5rem;max-width:410px;color:#ece4d8; }.as-speaker-image span { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.62rem;letter-spacing:.15em;color:#e1bc6a; }.as-speaker-image p { line-height:1.65; margin:1rem 0 0; font-size:.92rem; }
  .as-talks { background:#f0ebe0; color:#171511; padding:8rem 7.5vw; display:grid; grid-template-columns:.9fr 1.1fr; gap:9vw; }.as-talks .as-eyebrow { color:#a8782c; }.as-talk-list { border-top:1px solid #cfc7b9; }.as-talk-list article { display:grid; grid-template-columns:42px 1fr 38px; gap:1.4rem; padding:2rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid #cfc7b9; }.as-talk-list span { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.62rem;color:#a8782c; }.as-talk-list h3 { margin:0 0 .7rem; font-size:1.25rem; letter-spacing:-.04em; }.as-talk-list p { margin:0;color:#5c554c;font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.6; }.as-talk-list a { color:#171511; font-size:1.35rem; text-decoration:none; }
  .as-inquiry { background:#191816; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:8vw; padding:8rem 7.5vw; }.as-inquiry-copy { max-width:570px; }.as-inquiry .as-eyebrow { color:#e1bc6a; }.as-inquiry h2 { color:#f0e9de; }.as-inquiry-copy > p { color:#c8c0b5;line-height:1.65;font-size:1.02rem;margin:2rem 0;max-width:400px; }.as-inquiry-copy img { width:220px; aspect-ratio:4/5; object-fit:cover; display:block; margin-top:4rem; filter:saturate(.85); }.as-form { padding-top:1rem; }.as-form > p { color:#aaa196;font-size:.75rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 1.8rem; }.as-form label { display:block;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.59rem;letter-spacing:.11em;color:#c7bba9;margin:0 0 1.2rem; }.as-form input,.as-form textarea { width:100%;background:transparent;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid #5a554d;color:#f1eadd;padding:.75rem 0;font:400 .92rem 'DM Sans',sans-serif;outline:none; }.as-form input:focus,.as-form textarea:focus{border-color:#e1bc6a;}.as-form-pair { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.6rem; }.as-form button { width:100%;border:0;background:#e1bc6a;color:#171511;padding:1.1rem 1.2rem;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font:700 .64rem 'DM Sans',sans-serif;letter-spacing:.12em;cursor:pointer;margin-top:1rem; }.as-form button span {font-size:1rem;}.as-footer { display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:2rem;padding:1.8rem 3.2vw;background:#0e0d0c;color:#92897d;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:.53rem;letter-spacing:.11em; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .as-header { height:64px;padding:0 5vw;}.as-header nav{display:none}.as-wordmark{font-size:.66rem}.as-header-cta{font-size:.52rem;padding:.7rem .7rem}.as-hero{min-height:780px}.as-hero-image{object-position:64% center}.as-hero-overlay{background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(11,10,8,.94) 0%,rgba(11,10,8,.50) 77%),linear-gradient(0deg,rgba(11,10,8,.75),transparent 60%)}.as-hero-copy{width:100%;padding:0 6vw 5.2rem}.as-intro{max-width:335px;font-size:.94rem}.as-hero-side{display:none}.as-concept-note{padding:1.25rem 6vw;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.6rem}.as-outcomes,.as-story,.as-method,.as-talks,.as-inquiry{padding:5rem 6vw}.as-outcomes-head,.as-story,.as-talks,.as-inquiry{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2.5rem}.as-outcomes-head{padding:3rem 0}.as-outcomes-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.as-outcomes-grid article{padding:1.5rem 0;border-right:0;border-bottom:1px solid #d5cec1;min-height:auto;margin:0}.as-outcomes-grid h3{margin:1.5rem 0 .6rem}.as-method-top{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2rem;padding-bottom:2rem}.as-method-list{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.as-method-list article{min-height:190px;border-bottom:1px solid #38352f;padding:1.5rem 1rem 1.5rem 0}.as-method-list article+article{padding-left:1rem}.as-method-list h3{margin:2.4rem 0 .7rem}.as-speaker-image{min-height:560px}.as-speaker-image > img{object-position:65% center}.as-speaker-image > div{left:6vw;bottom:3rem;max-width:310px}.as-inquiry-copy img{margin-top:2rem}.as-form-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}.as-footer{padding:1.5rem 6vw;flex-direction:column;font-size:.49rem}.as-talk-list article{grid-template-columns:30px 1fr 24px} }
  @media (max-width: 420px) { h1{font-size:3.2rem}.as-method-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.as-method-list article,.as-method-list article+article{padding:1.5rem 0;border-right:0}.as-method-list h3{margin:1.6rem 0 .5rem} }
</style>
